  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Conservation of Biodiversity in China in the light of Climate Change</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This Project will feed into the implementation of the post 2020 Global Biodiversity Framework under the UN Convention on Biological Diversity (CBD), expected to be adopted at the 15th Conference of the Parties of the CBD in December 2022. Its main implementing partners include Nanjing Institute of Environmental Sciences under China&apos;s Ministry of Ecology and Environment, and Norwegian Environment Agency under the Norwegian Ministry of Climate and Environment. The project will promote transfer of knowledge and experiences between Norway and China, including but not limited to policies and measures for biodiversity conservation, climate change risk management, management of protected areas, restoration of ecosystems, protection of endangered species, and prevention and control of invasive alien species, and will further contribute to a new solution for biodiversity conservation in the context of climate change in China.</narrative>
  </description>
